1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,120
Has there been any contact with Count Mazurek?

2
00:00:04,480 --> 00:00:07,680
No. However, we know his landing castle is functional.

3
00:00:08,100 --> 00:00:12,560
If Itzalb Noah is still active, that means Count Mazurek is still among the living.

4
00:00:13,480 --> 00:00:16,860
Perhaps he is lying low and waiting for an opening, and is safe.

5
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:19,240
Or perhaps he's being held as a prisoner.

6
00:00:19,780 --> 00:00:23,260
Whichever it is, Mazurek's return does not seem likely.

7
00:00:24,120 --> 00:00:26,920
In which case, there is but one course of action.

8
00:00:26,920 --> 00:00:30,280
And what would that be?

9
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:36,100
I can no longer permit that Earth-born dog to run loose any longer.

10
00:00:56,920 --> 00:01:03,820
Thank you!

11
00:01:03,820 --> 00:01:33,800
Thank you.

12
00:01:33,820 --> 00:02:03,800
Thank you.

13
00:02:03,820 --> 00:02:05,820
Thank you.

14
00:02:33,820 --> 00:02:34,980
Yes, ma'am.

15
00:02:35,380 --> 00:02:36,860
And our Mars night guest?

16
00:02:37,140 --> 00:02:40,420
Not a word. It would seem he's one of the silent type.

17
00:02:40,860 --> 00:02:44,940
Mizusaki, do you know why they're so attractive to us? The silent type?

18
00:02:45,220 --> 00:02:47,600
Uh, because they seem calm and collected?

19
00:02:47,920 --> 00:02:50,300
Because they listen to whatever you have to say.

20
00:02:51,080 --> 00:02:52,100
And our replacement crew?

21
00:02:52,100 --> 00:02:53,980
Oh, yes, ma'am.

22
00:02:54,320 --> 00:02:55,460
All of them are on board.

23
00:02:55,900 --> 00:02:57,720
Station ships are revised to reflect that.

24
00:02:58,220 --> 00:03:00,160
A few of them served with us previously.

25
00:03:00,540 --> 00:03:02,480
Warrant Officer Kaisuka, Lieutenant Marito,

26
00:03:03,160 --> 00:03:07,400
as well as Dr. Yagarai, now an ensign, who is our official medical officer.

27
00:03:08,240 --> 00:03:12,660
Also, Ensign Kaisuka has a request to be able to interrogate the Mars night.

28
00:03:12,660 --> 00:03:17,360
And the reason for that is, he says he wants to try out his analytical engine.

29
00:03:20,120 --> 00:03:23,040
Really? You wrote the code for this yourself, Inaho?

30
00:03:23,420 --> 00:03:26,260
I just made some tweaks to the firmware it was already running.

31
00:03:26,260 --> 00:03:31,760
The connections here are somewhat expanded.

32
00:03:32,760 --> 00:03:33,820
How does it feel?

33
00:03:33,960 --> 00:03:34,940
Not all that different.

34
00:03:36,460 --> 00:03:39,020
You really shouldn't expand it any further than this.

35
00:03:39,440 --> 00:03:42,020
By the time you notice a problem, it'd be too late.

36
00:03:42,280 --> 00:03:44,600
I won't. I'm aware of the risk involved here.

37
00:03:46,920 --> 00:03:48,620
So, this is where you are.

38
00:03:50,740 --> 00:03:51,220
Yuki.

39
00:03:52,120 --> 00:03:53,080
Do you have a minute?

40
00:03:53,080 --> 00:03:57,780
Now, why did you agree to serve on this ship?

41
00:03:58,460 --> 00:03:59,740
What do you mean, why?

42
00:03:59,880 --> 00:04:00,760
There's no reason.

43
00:04:01,080 --> 00:04:03,360
It's not as if they're making you go on fighting.

44
00:04:04,060 --> 00:04:07,100
You should have packed up and gone away as soon as your wounds were all healed.

45
00:04:07,320 --> 00:04:09,300
It's exactly the same thing for you, too.

46
00:04:09,380 --> 00:04:10,580
It's absolutely not.

47
00:04:10,880 --> 00:04:12,360
Because I am a soldier.

48
00:04:12,840 --> 00:04:15,880
There was no valid reason for a young woman like you to be one.

49
00:04:16,080 --> 00:04:16,740
It's the same.

50
00:04:16,820 --> 00:04:17,660
It is not!

51
00:04:21,300 --> 00:04:22,740
I regret it every day.

52
00:04:23,320 --> 00:04:25,140
That I let you become a soldier.

53
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:29,760
But when I saw you unconscious and covered in blood,

54
00:04:30,580 --> 00:04:32,360
I asked myself,

55
00:04:32,900 --> 00:04:34,100
Why didn't I stop you?

56
00:04:34,860 --> 00:04:35,880
I became one.

57
00:04:36,600 --> 00:04:37,700
To protect you.

58
00:04:38,160 --> 00:04:41,780
I wanted to save you and the world you're such a wonderful part of.

59
00:04:41,780 --> 00:04:44,920
But I failed at it.

60
00:04:45,500 --> 00:04:46,340
I'm sorry.

61
00:04:47,660 --> 00:04:50,040
But you see, I can't just do nothing.

62
00:04:52,120 --> 00:04:53,620
Is it because of the princess?

63
00:04:55,520 --> 00:04:59,440
Because that girl is not the same princess you once knew.

64
00:04:59,440 --> 00:05:02,940
She's now an enemy who's trying to conquer the earth.

65
00:05:03,060 --> 00:05:04,220
That person is a fake.

66
00:05:04,560 --> 00:05:06,280
And the real one is still alive somewhere.

67
00:05:06,440 --> 00:05:08,200
Why would you possibly think that?

68
00:05:08,720 --> 00:05:10,240
Analysis by my left eye.

69
00:05:10,240 --> 00:05:13,340
All the facts add up.

70
00:05:13,680 --> 00:05:15,740
I think that she's being held against her will.

71
00:05:16,780 --> 00:05:19,480
Therefore, I want to rescue the princess.

72
00:05:19,840 --> 00:05:20,840
But that's impossible!

73
00:05:21,660 --> 00:05:22,260
Look, Yuki.

74
00:05:23,100 --> 00:05:25,480
She was in front of me, not more than a foot away.

75
00:05:26,620 --> 00:05:27,640
I was hurt.

76
00:05:28,240 --> 00:05:29,960
She was shot trying to help me.

77
00:05:29,960 --> 00:05:36,020
And that is why I have to save her.

78
00:05:37,020 --> 00:05:37,460
Now!

79
00:05:47,300 --> 00:05:48,480
Long time, Lieutenant.

80
00:05:50,700 --> 00:05:52,120
What condition are they in?

81
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:54,820
When they completed all the tests,

82
00:05:55,180 --> 00:05:58,040
diagnostics show those gravity waves really did a number on them.

83
00:05:58,040 --> 00:06:00,400
Most of them are going to need an overhaul.

84
00:06:00,940 --> 00:06:03,060
I understand that you're not drinking anymore.

85
00:06:03,900 --> 00:06:06,360
My primary physician is a real nag.

86
00:06:07,020 --> 00:06:09,760
In that case, I guess a toast is out of the question.

87
00:06:10,380 --> 00:06:12,600
Oh, a toast is always in order.

88
00:06:12,940 --> 00:06:14,260
You're just unbelievable.

89
00:06:14,780 --> 00:06:16,880
Hey, that comes straight from my doctor.

90
00:06:17,380 --> 00:06:18,380
Medicinal purposes.

91
00:06:21,680 --> 00:06:23,000
So, how are you feeling?

92
00:06:25,400 --> 00:06:27,120
Well, you don't look very happy.

93
00:06:27,120 --> 00:06:29,640
I heard you were given a full body search.

94
00:06:30,920 --> 00:06:34,540
I never conceived it possible to be subjected to such primitive questioning.

95
00:06:35,240 --> 00:06:38,560
We can't have you using a poison tooth or anything else like that.

96
00:06:39,200 --> 00:06:40,860
What an outdated notion.

97
00:06:41,180 --> 00:06:43,500
Says the knight battling for fame and glory.

98
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:45,300
From a Terran viewpoint,

99
00:06:45,820 --> 00:06:49,820
I suppose the feudal system of Verse would seem just as anachronistic.

100
00:06:50,200 --> 00:06:53,260
Well, if that is your problem, then why don't you just make a change?

101
00:06:53,260 --> 00:06:55,880
The words of one born into complacency.

102
00:06:56,380 --> 00:06:58,500
You're like pigs freezing to death.

103
00:06:58,980 --> 00:07:01,920
Once you are too cold to move, you've no chance of survival.

104
00:07:02,340 --> 00:07:03,400
You know a great deal.

105
00:07:03,840 --> 00:07:04,880
You admit I'm right?

106
00:07:05,460 --> 00:07:07,180
No, information about pigs.

107
00:07:07,860 --> 00:07:10,480
Princess Asalem had never even seen a bird before.

108
00:07:11,300 --> 00:07:13,600
Princess Asalem? You actually spoke to her?

109
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:15,200
We were on a ship together.

110
00:07:16,700 --> 00:07:17,600
I see.

111
00:07:18,520 --> 00:07:21,400
So you were one of those who sought to exploit her.

112
00:07:21,740 --> 00:07:23,800
Not exploitation. Cooperation.

113
00:07:24,520 --> 00:07:25,020
Cooperation?

114
00:07:25,900 --> 00:07:27,800
Would you just answer one question?

115
00:07:27,800 --> 00:07:34,020
Do I look like a man who would just blithely sell out his nation?

116
00:07:34,620 --> 00:07:37,240
You don't look like it, or sound like it.

117
00:07:37,640 --> 00:07:39,580
Which makes you the perfect man to ask.

118
00:07:41,080 --> 00:07:43,160
Did you swear an oath of loyalty?

119
00:07:43,160 --> 00:07:46,480
To Her Highness Princess Asalem?

120
00:07:46,480 --> 00:07:59,540
Aren't you going to eat anything, Rye?

121
00:07:59,740 --> 00:08:02,980
If you don't eat something, you won't have any energy if we go into combat.

122
00:08:03,680 --> 00:08:05,180
I'm just not very hungry.

123
00:08:05,440 --> 00:08:08,160
With a fasting diet, the weight comes off your boobs first.

124
00:08:08,300 --> 00:08:10,660
I've never been on a diet, so I wouldn't know about that.

125
00:08:10,660 --> 00:08:10,940
Huh?

126
00:08:11,400 --> 00:08:11,760
What?

127
00:08:12,880 --> 00:08:15,180
You mean you've never ever tried to lose weight?

128
00:08:15,180 --> 00:08:17,500
That's amazing!

129
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:20,400
How do you keep that trim figure of yours?

130
00:08:20,720 --> 00:08:22,880
Yes, please. I'd like to know that too.

131
00:08:24,680 --> 00:08:25,120
Commander!

132
00:08:25,660 --> 00:08:27,040
Are you having lunch here, ma'am?

133
00:08:27,560 --> 00:08:31,380
Since we're in port, I thought it might be a nice change to eat somewhere other than the ship.

134
00:08:31,620 --> 00:08:34,060
You're right about that. We don't get to eat out much.

135
00:08:34,400 --> 00:08:35,720
Oh yeah, that reminds me.

136
00:08:36,540 --> 00:08:38,120
Has anyone seen Inaho today?

137
00:08:38,120 --> 00:08:41,180
I was going to ask him to join us, but he was already gone.

138
00:08:41,500 --> 00:08:44,860
Ensign Kaiska is busy. He's interrogating the Mars Knight at the moment.

139
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:47,500
Huh? Inaho is doing that?

140
00:08:48,300 --> 00:08:49,660
I think I'll head back.

141
00:08:50,200 --> 00:08:52,100
Hey! Wait a minute! Hold on a sec!

142
00:08:52,380 --> 00:08:53,100
Hey, Rae!

143
00:08:53,100 --> 00:08:57,740
She never said the secret to her figure.

144
00:08:58,540 --> 00:09:05,880
So what you're telling me is that the Princess Asalem currently at our moon base is not her, but actually an imposter?

145
00:09:06,880 --> 00:09:07,400
Yes.

146
00:09:07,400 --> 00:09:11,880
If true, then where might one find the real Princess Asalem?

147
00:09:12,540 --> 00:09:14,400
Being held as a prisoner somewhere?

148
00:09:15,480 --> 00:09:18,520
Or is there some other reason she cannot show herself?

149
00:09:18,680 --> 00:09:20,180
Possibly both those things.

150
00:09:20,180 --> 00:09:22,360
Your left eye determined that as well?

151
00:09:22,900 --> 00:09:24,220
It's an analytical engine.

152
00:09:30,900 --> 00:09:36,960
Unfortunately, I am not one who is so foolish as to believe such a preposterous tale as that one.

153
00:09:37,280 --> 00:09:39,660
We've retrieved your cataphract and are studying it.

154
00:09:39,660 --> 00:09:45,180
The force of that explosion knocked the old Noah drive offline.

155
00:09:45,440 --> 00:09:47,860
It's a pity it will never be able to function again.

156
00:09:48,140 --> 00:09:49,920
You powered it down yourself, didn't you?

157
00:09:50,480 --> 00:09:51,940
Out of fear that we would steal it.

158
00:09:51,940 --> 00:09:55,320
I told you it stopped working after the explosion.

159
00:09:55,920 --> 00:09:56,880
Did it really?

160
00:09:57,780 --> 00:09:58,140
No.

161
00:09:58,420 --> 00:09:59,920
You intentionally shut it down.

162
00:10:01,860 --> 00:10:03,440
I will say it again.

163
00:10:04,680 --> 00:10:07,260
That is not the real Princess Asalem.

164
00:10:09,780 --> 00:10:12,320
There are many species of birds as well.

165
00:10:13,180 --> 00:10:16,680
There are large birds, and some that are very small.

166
00:10:17,420 --> 00:10:18,800
Others have brilliant colors.

167
00:10:21,940 --> 00:10:26,020
And this is how they fly.

168
00:10:26,380 --> 00:10:28,000
Through the open skies of Earth.

169
00:10:28,460 --> 00:10:30,800
While most birds are fully capable of flying,

170
00:10:31,240 --> 00:10:34,360
there are some that are flightless and remain Earth-bound.

171
00:10:34,820 --> 00:10:36,200
Birds that can't fly?

172
00:10:36,700 --> 00:10:38,240
Princess Asalem might say

173
00:10:38,240 --> 00:10:41,620
that she finds it sad that they cannot fly

174
00:10:41,620 --> 00:10:43,540
even though they are equipped with wings.

175
00:10:44,140 --> 00:10:45,300
She is so kind.

176
00:10:45,980 --> 00:10:48,040
She feels very deeply for others.

177
00:10:48,220 --> 00:10:48,860
Not to worry.

178
00:10:49,160 --> 00:10:50,820
The flightless ones do not miss it.

179
00:10:51,940 --> 00:10:54,880
The ones to pity are those who can fly,

180
00:10:55,080 --> 00:10:56,220
but are kept in cages.

181
00:10:57,160 --> 00:10:59,600
Why would anyone trap them like that?

182
00:11:01,360 --> 00:11:02,240
Because...

183
00:11:02,240 --> 00:11:05,320
They are so very beautiful.

184
00:11:05,320 --> 00:11:15,020
Princess Asalem was shot right in front of me.

185
00:11:15,700 --> 00:11:18,100
And Count Sosbom was the man who did it.

186
00:11:18,240 --> 00:11:19,480
That's preposterous.

187
00:11:19,600 --> 00:11:21,980
At that point, he left with slain Troyard,

188
00:11:22,520 --> 00:11:24,620
taking Princess Asalem along with them.

189
00:11:25,800 --> 00:11:28,800
Count Sosbom is celebrated as the great hero

190
00:11:28,800 --> 00:11:30,600
who rescued Princess Asalem.

191
00:11:30,600 --> 00:11:32,840
He's anything but a hero.

192
00:11:34,280 --> 00:11:37,260
He's the mastermind who planned out her assassination.

193
00:11:37,820 --> 00:11:39,620
No, that cannot be the case.

194
00:11:39,980 --> 00:11:41,740
Those bastards tricked my father,

195
00:11:41,900 --> 00:11:43,580
made him their pawn, and used him.

196
00:11:44,020 --> 00:11:46,060
Then they crushed him like a bug.

197
00:11:46,460 --> 00:11:48,380
So, you were verse-born then.

198
00:11:48,380 --> 00:11:50,560
I see.

199
00:11:51,240 --> 00:11:52,180
In any event,

200
00:11:52,300 --> 00:11:54,940
your father would have certainly died sooner or later.

201
00:11:55,420 --> 00:11:57,780
You should give thanks that he wasn't branded a traitor

202
00:11:57,780 --> 00:11:59,600
and summarily lynched or worse.

203
00:11:59,800 --> 00:12:01,060
What's that supposed to mean?

204
00:12:01,060 --> 00:12:05,540
Are you saying that my father deserved to die?

205
00:12:06,160 --> 00:12:06,940
Let's go.

206
00:12:07,600 --> 00:12:09,020
I'm not done with him.

207
00:12:10,100 --> 00:12:11,100
Come with me.

208
00:12:13,800 --> 00:12:14,820
Let go!

209
00:12:17,860 --> 00:12:19,440
You must think I'm an idiot.

210
00:12:22,440 --> 00:12:24,420
Then I'll always be bound by the past.

211
00:12:24,800 --> 00:12:25,960
Always be its prisoner.

212
00:12:27,360 --> 00:12:28,300
Well, you're right.

213
00:12:28,360 --> 00:12:29,520
I am just like them.

214
00:12:29,520 --> 00:12:32,040
All I do is blame others.

215
00:12:32,760 --> 00:12:33,540
I hate them.

216
00:12:33,780 --> 00:12:34,560
I envy them.

217
00:12:35,340 --> 00:12:37,120
Fight and steal and kill them!

218
00:12:38,040 --> 00:12:39,560
Just a stupid Martian.

219
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:41,200
No, you are different.

220
00:12:41,740 --> 00:12:42,720
I am not.

221
00:12:43,060 --> 00:12:43,660
You are.

222
00:12:43,860 --> 00:12:44,760
I am not.

223
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:45,620
You are.

224
00:12:45,960 --> 00:12:47,320
I'm no different than them!

225
00:12:47,420 --> 00:12:48,520
I hate Martians!

226
00:12:50,520 --> 00:12:53,460
And I hate myself more than all of them!

227
00:12:59,520 --> 00:13:01,740
Count Marilsian, you say?

228
00:13:02,160 --> 00:13:02,820
Yes, sir.

229
00:13:03,180 --> 00:13:04,400
He has been calling repeatedly.

230
00:13:04,840 --> 00:13:07,500
He is saying that he wishes to be put through to Princess Asalem.

231
00:13:08,220 --> 00:13:10,380
And what does Sir Slain have to say?

232
00:13:10,740 --> 00:13:12,680
I have been unable to find the Count, sir.

233
00:13:13,300 --> 00:13:14,620
What is this commotion?

234
00:13:14,620 --> 00:13:19,520
Leave us.

235
00:13:19,780 --> 00:13:20,360
Yes, sir.

236
00:13:22,580 --> 00:13:23,460
I see.

237
00:13:23,800 --> 00:13:26,000
Can you not have your discussion with me present?

238
00:13:26,400 --> 00:13:27,240
Sorry, Your Highness.

239
00:13:28,180 --> 00:13:32,320
Unfortunately, even here at the Moonbase, knowledge of your existence is somewhat limited.

240
00:13:32,920 --> 00:13:34,620
Please try to avoid public areas.

241
00:13:35,080 --> 00:13:36,800
Do you think I should speak with him?

242
00:13:36,800 --> 00:13:40,180
It is Count Marilsian, isn't it?

243
00:13:40,940 --> 00:13:41,800
But Your Highness...

244
00:13:42,580 --> 00:13:43,740
Is there a problem?

245
00:13:47,920 --> 00:13:49,940
Patch him through to the throne room.

246
00:13:53,200 --> 00:13:57,100
Her Royal Highness Princess Asalem is most exceedingly gracious.

247
00:13:57,900 --> 00:14:00,040
I beg forgiveness for this disturbance.

248
00:14:00,680 --> 00:14:02,840
Lord Count Marilsian, what a great pleasure.

249
00:14:03,360 --> 00:14:06,560
So now then, what was it that you wished to discuss with me?

250
00:14:06,800 --> 00:14:09,240
To contact me without Count Troyard's leave.

251
00:14:09,500 --> 00:14:11,020
Well, it must be very urgent.

252
00:14:11,320 --> 00:14:11,540
Hm.

253
00:14:12,840 --> 00:14:14,120
It is indeed.

254
00:14:14,900 --> 00:14:17,760
Is his permission required to speak with you, Your Highness?

255
00:14:18,420 --> 00:14:24,300
It seems to be quite overprotective for Count Troyard to keep you essentially under guard like this.

256
00:14:25,520 --> 00:14:27,700
Not the best choice of words, perhaps.

257
00:14:28,700 --> 00:14:33,400
Let us then say instead he is a knight protecting his princess in her ivory tower.

258
00:14:33,400 --> 00:14:39,120
My deepest apologies if I have given offense, comparing Your Highness to a bird in a cage.

259
00:14:39,760 --> 00:14:41,160
A bird in a cage?

260
00:14:41,620 --> 00:14:46,520
As I understand it, an expression used on Earth to describe when deprived of her freedom.

261
00:14:49,040 --> 00:14:50,420
Message from base command.

262
00:14:50,800 --> 00:14:52,500
They say that the prisoner has escaped.

263
00:14:52,620 --> 00:14:53,620
Put the ship on alert.

264
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:55,280
Notify all duty stations.

265
00:14:55,280 --> 00:14:56,200
Yes, ma'am.

266
00:15:11,120 --> 00:15:13,060
I hate these late-night alarms.

267
00:15:13,600 --> 00:15:15,060
They're just killing me.

268
00:15:16,340 --> 00:15:17,020
Raiyei.

269
00:15:18,100 --> 00:15:19,900
Come on, time to get the lead out.

270
00:15:22,280 --> 00:15:22,920
Raiyei?

271
00:15:22,920 --> 00:15:27,820
So, it's you.

272
00:15:28,580 --> 00:15:29,360
Come on.

273
00:15:38,360 --> 00:15:39,540
Let's get out of here.

274
00:15:39,540 --> 00:15:48,580
Why are you doing this for me?

275
00:15:49,220 --> 00:15:54,460
I want you to go back to your landing castle so you can find out where the real Princess of Salem is being held.

276
00:15:55,740 --> 00:15:57,720
But why would you trust me?

277
00:15:58,120 --> 00:16:01,580
Because I believe you want the same thing Princess of Salem does.

278
00:16:01,580 --> 00:16:07,020
I don't think you ever had any desire to attack the Earth like this.

279
00:16:08,080 --> 00:16:09,880
Your left eye told you that?

280
00:16:10,060 --> 00:16:12,840
I can tell that much without ever using my left eye.

281
00:16:13,580 --> 00:16:16,240
You have made yourself very familiar with the Earth.

282
00:16:16,960 --> 00:16:18,420
Not for invasion purposes.

283
00:16:19,300 --> 00:16:20,700
Your interest lies elsewhere.

284
00:16:20,700 --> 00:16:23,680
Ah, so you do see everything.

285
00:16:24,420 --> 00:16:27,000
There's one other thing I want you to find out for me.

286
00:16:29,040 --> 00:16:30,460
Slain Troyart's objective.

287
00:16:30,760 --> 00:16:31,480
What's his plan?

288
00:16:34,420 --> 00:16:37,040
Keep on a north heading and you'll reach your landing castle.

289
00:16:37,600 --> 00:16:38,900
You'll need to walk from here.

290
00:16:38,900 --> 00:16:39,540
Yes.

291
00:16:41,040 --> 00:16:41,520
Here.

292
00:16:44,520 --> 00:16:45,480
Food and water.

293
00:16:46,120 --> 00:16:48,900
We can't have you dying of thirst before you can make it away.

294
00:16:49,720 --> 00:16:52,520
Though truthfully, that wouldn't bother me one little bit.

295
00:16:52,740 --> 00:16:57,520
If it comes to it, understand that Princess of Salem's well-being may be in your hands.

296
00:17:00,280 --> 00:17:03,160
Before I leave here, might I ask you one thing?

297
00:17:03,160 --> 00:17:05,680
What is your name?

298
00:17:06,820 --> 00:17:12,340
My name is Count Mazurek, a proud member of the 37 clans of the Verse Empire.

299
00:17:12,860 --> 00:17:14,120
Count Mazurek, huh?

300
00:17:15,100 --> 00:17:18,160
There's a type of folk music on Earth with a similar name.

301
00:17:18,760 --> 00:17:19,100
Yes.

302
00:17:19,720 --> 00:17:24,620
As I researched the meaning behind my name, I became more and more fascinated with the Earth.

303
00:17:25,960 --> 00:17:27,180
What is your name?

304
00:17:28,180 --> 00:17:28,860
I'm Inaho.

305
00:17:31,060 --> 00:17:32,240
Inaho Kaizuka.

306
00:17:33,160 --> 00:17:38,680
Count Mazurek, take good care of Princess of Salem.

307
00:17:39,880 --> 00:17:40,920
I shall do so.

308
00:17:42,140 --> 00:17:43,300
Inaho Kaizuka.

309
00:17:45,880 --> 00:17:46,200
Hmm.

310
00:17:49,080 --> 00:17:52,020
Tell me, why'd you ask me to help with this?

311
00:17:52,460 --> 00:17:53,180
What do you mean?

312
00:17:53,960 --> 00:17:56,760
Didn't you stop to think that I might just kill that Martian?

313
00:17:57,720 --> 00:17:59,140
Like I did with the Princess?

314
00:17:59,940 --> 00:18:02,660
I need to point out that you did not in fact kill her.

315
00:18:03,160 --> 00:18:04,520
I failed to kill her.

316
00:18:04,680 --> 00:18:05,580
You're different now.

317
00:18:05,880 --> 00:18:06,620
I am not.

318
00:18:06,700 --> 00:18:07,140
You are.

319
00:18:07,460 --> 00:18:08,280
Give it a rest.

320
00:18:08,460 --> 00:18:09,180
I am not.

321
00:18:09,200 --> 00:18:09,820
You are.

322
00:18:09,820 --> 00:18:14,540
You are no longer the person you were then.

323
00:18:18,540 --> 00:18:20,200
Mustang leader to Mustang 1-1.

324
00:18:20,400 --> 00:18:21,260
What's your status?

325
00:18:22,380 --> 00:18:23,380
Mustang 1-1.

326
00:18:23,580 --> 00:18:24,060
All good.

327
00:18:24,540 --> 00:18:25,220
Stay on alert.

328
00:18:26,120 --> 00:18:26,820
Roger that.

329
00:18:26,820 --> 00:18:27,480
I know.

330
00:18:27,480 --> 00:18:31,880
I know.

331
00:18:31,880 --> 00:18:32,220
Why?

332
00:18:32,220 --> 00:18:32,720
Why?

333
00:18:33,540 --> 00:18:34,260
Why?

334
00:18:44,260 --> 00:18:45,680
What's the meaning of this?

335
00:18:45,960 --> 00:18:48,740
Who authorized those landing castles to dock here?

336
00:18:48,740 --> 00:18:51,160
My lord, it was...

337
00:18:51,160 --> 00:18:52,720
I authorized them to.

338
00:18:52,720 --> 00:18:53,720
Your highness.

339
00:18:55,080 --> 00:18:59,840
Counts Marilsian and Barocruz requested personal audience with Princess of Salem.

340
00:19:00,560 --> 00:19:02,060
So I permitted them to dock.

341
00:19:03,240 --> 00:19:04,920
First as Princess of Salem.

342
00:19:05,680 --> 00:19:07,720
But then...

343
00:19:07,720 --> 00:19:09,660
As the rightful Princess of Verse.

344
00:19:09,780 --> 00:19:11,200
Why would you do such a thing?

345
00:19:11,200 --> 00:19:14,680
Let's be off now.

346
00:19:15,640 --> 00:19:18,740
It would be poor behavior to keep our visitors waiting.

347
00:19:18,740 --> 00:19:48,720
Let's be off now.

348
00:19:48,740 --> 00:19:52,900
Princess of Salem.

349
00:19:53,100 --> 00:19:59,000
We are both humbled and delighted that your highness would grant us an audience on such extremely short notice.

350
00:19:59,280 --> 00:20:06,980
My lord, Count Marilsian, and my lord, Count Barocruz, I am most grateful to my faithful knights for our orbital defenses.

351
00:20:08,380 --> 00:20:12,700
If times were normal, I expect you would go down to Earth and expand your domains.

352
00:20:12,700 --> 00:20:16,180
We leave the conquest of Earth in the hands of our like-minded brethren.

353
00:20:16,800 --> 00:20:18,680
Your highness needn't worry on that account.

354
00:20:19,480 --> 00:20:21,260
I see. That is good to hear.

355
00:20:21,260 --> 00:20:25,120
If your highness permits, there is a matter of greater importance to address.

356
00:20:25,560 --> 00:20:34,080
With the terrible, tragic death of Count Sosbohm, who will succeed as commander of the Royal Guard charged with protecting the Moonbase and your highness?

357
00:20:34,080 --> 00:20:37,640
You needn't worry about any of that, Count Marilsian.

358
00:20:37,640 --> 00:20:40,640
I shall assume those duties without delay.

359
00:20:42,700 --> 00:20:51,280
Princess of Salem, I have come to beg you to consider if you would do me the honor of allowing me to serve at your side.

360
00:20:51,280 --> 00:20:53,800
I have already told you, Count Marilsian.

361
00:20:53,800 --> 00:20:58,480
I will thank you to keep your lowborn comments to yourself, Terran.

362
00:20:58,480 --> 00:21:04,100
This is a fortress under the flag of the Verse Empire.

363
00:21:04,100 --> 00:21:12,060
If I lost the post to someone like Count Sosbohm, a man of great warrior merit, who rescued her highness, I could approve.

364
00:21:12,700 --> 00:21:20,120
Yet you, who remains a Terran, even if you are his adopted son, actually think that holy post should be yours?

365
00:21:20,120 --> 00:21:28,920
The very thought that one of low blood is setting foot inside the castle where a member of the Verse Imperial family dwells is intolerable.

366
00:21:29,480 --> 00:21:32,900
One without a landing castle is unfit to call himself Count.

367
00:21:37,400 --> 00:21:41,060
